The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
ret = snprintf(dst, rest(dst, end), "\"%s\"%s", val, vnode->next ? ", " : "\n");
```
```c
ret = snprintf(dst, rest(dst, end), "\"%s\"\n", val);
```
Reason:
The code did not account for the presence of double quote characters in the `val` string. As a result, when `val` contained a double quote, it was incorrectly enclosed in double quotes again, leading to improperly formatted output.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (strchr(val, '"'))
    q = '\'';
else
    q = '"';
ret = snprintf(dst, rest(dst, end), "%c%s%c%s", q, val, q, vnode->next ? ", " : "\n");
```
```c
ret = snprintf(dst, rest(dst, end), "\"\"\n");
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a check for double quotes in the `val` string. If a double quote is found, it uses single quotes for enclosing the value; otherwise, it uses double quotes. This ensures that the output is correctly formatted regardless of the presence of double quotes in the value.

